# Line endings: LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. A shell
# script checked out with CRLF fails inside the Linux containers and on the server
# ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r'"), and the Dockerfile, Caddyfile and SQL migrations
# are read on Linux too. Prettier writes LF as well (its default endOfLine).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never converted or diffed as text. Listed explicitly rather than left to detection, so a
# font or workbook that happens to look like text is still never rewritten.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
